This is just a question of style.  I think that it's at least worth
finding an altar and testing out the curse status first.  OTOH, if
you carry potions and scrolls around without a container you may 
end up losing them to fire traps or similar hazards.  So there has
to be some kind of happy medium.  I don't like to mess with potions
if I don't have a way to cure blindness, hallucination, confusion,
etc.  Since I always find a way to do that and an altar ASAP, I don't 
think the wait is that big a deal.  

If you're a new player and you don't know what all the funny 
identifying messages correspond to, then I recommend waiting for
identify scrolls, which are identified by #chatting to shopkeepers
and knowing your prices.  Otherwise it's just a question of how 
conservatively you play.  Once I've got most of the stuff identified,
I tend to have enough scrolls or spells to identify the few remaining
items I find later.  It becomes more important then, since it's   
usually something rarer that you may want to ensure is blessed before
you read / drink it.  Don't want to waste something like a scroll 
of genocide, a potion of gain ability, or a potion of gain level.

